# Always Use Tailwind for New UI Code

All new UI code in this repo must use Tailwind CSS via the `/tw` Ragnar imports. Never introduce or extend Fela / styled-system styling.

## When editing an existing Fela-styled file

If a file uses Fela `extend={...}` or styled-system props (`m="space2"`, `bg="primary"`, etc.) and you're touching it for any reason, opportunistically migrate the elements you touch to Tailwind — even when the change isn't styling-related. Keep the diff minimal: migrate the touched element, not untouched siblings.

When adding new styling, never extend the Fela code; use Tailwind from the start.

If the surrounding component is genuinely too complex to migrate cleanly in scope, ask the user before either keeping the existing Fela or adding new.

That's how Fela usage shrinks rather than spreads.

## Mechanics

- Import Ragnar components from their `/tw` subpath (e.g. `@mentimeter/ragnar-ui/box/tw`, `@mentimeter/ragnar-ui/text/tw`).
- Use `clsx` from `@mentimeter/ragnar-tailwind-config` when composing 4+ classes or any conditional className.
- Before guessing token mappings, load the tailwind-migration skill (`.claude/skills/tailwind-migration/SKILL.md`) — this repo has custom design tokens that diverge from stock Tailwind.

## Examples

Bad — matching nearby Fela in the same file:

```tsx
import { Box } from '@mentimeter/ragnar-ui/box';

<Box extend={({ theme }) => ({ marginRight: `${theme.kosmosSpacing.space2}px` })} />
```

Good — Tailwind via `/tw` import:

```tsx
import { Box } from '@mentimeter/ragnar-ui/box/tw';

<Box className="mr-2" />
```
